<font color="#993322">

<table align='CENTER' cellpadding='2' border='1' cellspacing='2' background='http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif'><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=8&y=2003">This Month</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=7&y=2003">July-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=6&y=2003">June-2003</A></TD></TR><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=5&y=2003">May-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=4&y=2003">April-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=3&y=2003">March-2003</A></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><CENTER><font size=+2>March, 2003</font><BR></center><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>PoF & Sornae</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Monday - March 31st 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Congrats Sornae!! First enchanter epic earned within Legerdemain.  Very nice accomplishment indeed.  I hope you're proud of yourself, cuz I certainly am proud of you.  I'm sure the final snagging of the Shissar with 5 people had to have been a heart-poundingly fun adventure!  Sorry I wasn't there to see it, but I hope to see you at the forefront of many more successful raids and strikes.<BR>
<BR>
Big gratz!</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Lot of events!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Monday - March 31st 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Thanks, everyone who's been running and attending the many and varied events.  Sornae's PoH/PoF, Ketrel with BoT/PoN hedge, Kabniel in PoN caves, Erryn's epic adventure in the hole, etc.  It makes me happy to see so many taking up the call and helping to make our EQ adventures much more entertaining from day to day.<BR>
<BR>
As we move forward, I hope to see more and more of these events.  In it all, I hope that any failures are taken with a grain of salt.  Failures are what make us grow in experience, knowledge, and what make success that much more sweet.  Don't let them be too discouraging.  Of course, we haven't had much need to worry about that lately, but I'm sure it will eventually happen :P~</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>WTG Sornae!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Saturday - March 22nd 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Sornae's first event leadership.  PoHate use to be one of the end-all zones.  Tough to break in to, tough to fight in, and especially tough to avoid trains in.  Considering the expansions since then, it's not quite the place it use to be.  Still, it's certainly not the easiest zone in EQ.  The zone should be getting a revamp in the near future, but I'm glad to say that Sornae had a chance to hit the original zone before it changed.<BR>
She took about 2 groups up initially and it eventually grew to 3 groups. Moobley got his final epic piece, Sornae got the vamp dust she was after, 2 hands of maestro dropped (gratz Far and MQ), and Inny got ownt.<BR>
<center><a href="http://www.guild-legerdemain.com/memberfiles/user1/InnysDead1a.jpg" target="_inny"><img  border=0 src="http://www.guild-legerdemain.com/memberfiles/user1/InnysDead1b.jpg"></A></center><BR>
Suprisingly enough, it was the very first time Legerdemain killed him as a guild.  Thanks for the awesome event, Sornae, and I hope to see you running more in the future.</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>And downward we plunge</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Saturday - March 15th 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Just after we accomplish the largest task Legerdemain has ever tried, we start losing members. Xanamech Nexmirthafen, the Dragon of PoInnovation, recently fell to our will. He max hit for 1390points.  He cast an AE direct damage spell for 800.  He also cast an AE stun/dd spell for 300ish a pop.  I believe he had about 150,000 hit points.  Not an easy target to say the least.  Certainly not an easy target for a guild who's never even killed Gorenaire; a dragon who max hits for about 520HP, has 32,000 hit points, and AE slows with the possibly CH. Of course, I believe her AE hits for 750hp, and she also has that dragon fear and dispell thing going.  Still, she's level 60 and quite the punk in comparrsion to a dragon like the level 66 Xanamech Nexmirthafen.<BR>
<BR>
Well, we kilt him good, and apparently whet some appetites.  We lost Gann, Far, and Bubben. Gann was the only one who listed reasons that you can read in our Foyer.  Chief among them seemed to be that we don't raid enough or kill enough in uber places of EQ.  His whetted appetite required more than what Legerdemain could provide to quench.  Apparently there was nothing to do but leave the guild. After my response, and a few others, to Gann's goodbye post, Farlander and Bubben weren't driven to be so open with their reasoning. Not that they needed a reason, mind you.<BR>
<BR>
I'll miss each of them, as I have missed Deyna and Wuddar.  Merciless and Taetianna will also not be seen much if at all.  Their reasoning is certainly different but the effect is the same.  Hryin has found new fun.  EQ no longer holds the same joy it once did for him. It happens.<BR>
<BR>
So as Legerdemain reaches a new height, we fall.  How many more will be leaving?  I do not know.  I'm sure many whetted appetites are chomping at the bit.  Our forces are now weakened and have little if any hope of continuing our upward trend anytime in the near future.  It's like giving everyone a steak, and when it's half eatten, pulling it away.  To be able to move upward again, to keep progressing within the game, we must again re-enforce our numbers.  How many will leave in the interrum?  Will Legerdemain ever be able to reach the meager goals that we just left behind? I don't know.<BR>
<BR>
I do know that I play this game for fun, and that I will continue to do so.  It is disheartening to know, however, that when we reach such heights, accomplish the goals we set for ourselves, the effect will mearly be self distructive.  That is, assuming history repeats itself in this manner. The whole situation does remind me of <a href="http://www.bygosh.com/Aesop/dogreflection.htm">a similar story</a>, though.</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>PoI Dragon</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Sunday - March 9th 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Well, Well, Well, For our first shot at this dragon I was VERY impressed, everything went very smooth.  We started a bit late but made up for it by getting done at about 12:45 EST.  We did not get flagged because the dragon killed the little gnome but, we did get two Very Nice items.  Next time I think if we keep the MA alive, we will all get flagged for the factory.  The gnome died in between Farlander's death and Grimmice taking agro I believe.  We will get flagged next time though :).  Thanks everyone who attended, it was a very successful raid
<BR>
<BR>
<u>Farlander</u><BR>
Cord Hilted Spike driver
<BR>
<u>Embren</u><BR>
Pulsing Phase Emitter</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:fishfish029@hotmail.com>Bubben</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>New Probation</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Monday - March 3rd 2003</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Popular demand has ruled that a probationary period will be added to our <a href=" http://pub148.ezboard.com/flegerdemainfrm22.showMessage?topicID=1.topic">application process</A>.  A second vote will be initiated 3 weeks after an applicant is accepted in to the guild.  One week later, the new membership will continue or halt based on the results of that 2nd vote.  Our hope is that the additional vote will allow us to more quickly weed out those who readily prove to us they are not Legerdemain material shortly after being accepted.<BR>
Members can feel free to post any additional thoughts and feelings on the subject <a href="http://pub148.ezboard.com/flegerdemainfrm5.showMessage?topicID=587.topic">here</a>.</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR>



</font>
</TD>
